<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore oil export value up 29.2 pct in Nov YoY.</title>
<headline>Singapore oil export value up 29.2 pct in Nov YoY.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The value of Singapore's oil exports in November jumped 29.2 percent to S$1.466 billion from November 1995, the Singapore Trade Development Board said on Friday.</p>
<p>The November value was also 9.1 percent higher than in October, when exports were valued at S$1.344 billion, the data showed.</p>
<p>The TDB said the year-on-year growth &quot;was due mainly to the continued increase of oil prices, by 25 percent as compared to a year ago&quot;.  </p>
<p>Crude and product prices have been rising throughout 1996 largely as a result of a draw down in stocks by key consuming areas North American and Europe.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3081)</p>
